Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos7870-on7xelte: describe the TD4300 panel reset and supplies

Origin: j7prime touch investigation (not upstream). Base: Linux v7.3.4 +
patches 0001-0004. OPTIONAL: built as a separate DTB variant; do not use
for the first touch tests.

Upstream gives the TD4300 panel only backlight-gpios, so panel-synaptics-tddi
gets dummy vio/vsn/vsp supplies and no reset line and can never power-cycle
or reset the TDDI chip (display + touch). Samsung's DT for on7xelte
(exynos7870-on7xelte_common.dtsi, decon_board) uses:
  LCD_1P8 = PMIC LDO30 (vio), gpio_panel_enp = gpd3-7, gpio_panel_enn = gpd4-0,
  gpio_lcd_rst = gpd3-4 (pulse high-low-high), gpio_blic_on = gpd3-5.
Describe those so blank/unblank really re-initialises the chip. Because the
reset line is shared by display and touch on a TDDI, every panel prepare also
resets the touch controller; rmi4 recovers through the F01 attention handler
only if F01 is bound (needs 0001/0002 first). Both regulators are
regulator-boot-on so the bootloader's state is kept at probe.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-on7xelte.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-on7xelte.dts
@@ -83,6 +83,25 @@
 		enable-active-high;
 	};
 
+	/* TDDI panel bias: ISL98611 positive/negative output enables (ENP/ENN) */
+	vsn_panel: regulator-panel-vsn {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "panel_vsn";
+		gpio = <&gpd4 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+		regulator-boot-on;
+		startup-delay-us = <10000>;
+	};
+
+	vsp_panel: regulator-panel-vsp {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "panel_vsp";
+		gpio = <&gpd3 7 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+		regulator-boot-on;
+		startup-delay-us = <2000>;
+	};
+
 	reserved-memory {
 		#address-cells = <2>;
 		#size-cells = <1>;
@@ -131,6 +150,11 @@
 		reg = <0>;
 
 		backlight-gpios = <&gpd3 5 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+		reset-gpios = <&gpd3 4 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+
+		vio-supply = <&vdd_ldo30>;
+		vsn-supply = <&vsn_panel>;
+		vsp-supply = <&vsp_panel>;
 
 		width-mm = <68>;
 		height-mm = <121>;
